 "text": "9/29/26, 9:41 AM\ne Alternatively, you can configure it for a download for mobile data entry (MDE).\n\nIn Customizing under |*SAP Utilities + Customer Service } Process Execution  Move-In/Out  Move-Out > Define Move-Out\nControl Parameters at Contract Level J, you can also configure the way in which meter reading orders that were created in the\n\nmove-out are further processed.\n\nFeatures\n\nWhen you create a move-out, the system proposes an existing meter reading result for all the billing-relevant registers allocated to\n\nthe installation for billing purposes. Ensure you have configured the system accordingly in Customizing under |}*SAP Utilities\nDevice Management \u00bb Meter Reading \u00bb Basic Settings \u00bb Define Control Parameters for Meter Reading Data Processing\n\ne Ifthe system proposes a meter reading result then choose one of the following two options:\no If you adopt the meter reading result, the system adds the meter reading reason End to the result.\n\no If you change the meter reading result, a new result is created with the meter reading reason End.\n\ne Ifthe system does not propose a meter reading result, you can have it estimate a result or enter one manually. In both\ncases, the system creates a new result with the meter reading reason Move-in.\n\ne If aresult is not created by your adopting/changing a proposed result, and if you do not enter one manually, the system\ncreates a service notification or service order for the register. For more information see Service notifications and orders.\n\nAutomatic Estimation of Meter Reading Results During Move-Out\n\nIf a contract is terminated when a supply scenario is created or changed, you can have missing meter readings estimated\nautomatically when you create the move-out.\n\nIf you want to use this function, create an implementation for method STOP_CONTRACT of business add-in (BAdlI)\nISU_IDE_DRGSCEN_GEN.\n\nFor more information, see the documentation for the BAdI.\n\nIf you want to use the function for automatically estimating missing meter readings during move-out in the master data generator,\nadjust your master data templates as follows in Customizing for SAP Utilities under |Customer Service } Master Data\n\nGenerator \u00bb Define Master Data Template\n\nAttribute ESTIMATE_MR (Master data generator: Estimate MR Results During Move-Out) must contain the value \"X in all nodes\nof the master data template category MOVE_OUT (Move-Out in Connection with CRM).\n",
